4. Upstream Sources and Other Components

4.1 Rockchip Linux kernel source

The Ampheck Eidos Alpha kernel is built from the public Rockchip Linux kernel
repository, pinned to a fixed commit on the develop-6.1 branch:

  Repository: https://github.com/rockchip-linux/kernel.git
  Branch: develop-6.1
  Commit: 77168c8d5ab82399f65a80e9f807b50ba37cf483
  Version: Linux 6.1.172

The exact source revision is fetched from the official repository at build
time into the generated kernel tree. This SDK does not publish or redistribute
kernel source archives. Board integration consists of the Ampheck defconfig,
device tree, and board kernel patch series in this repository:

  boards/ampheck/eidos-alpha/kernel/eidos_alpha_defconfig
  boards/ampheck/eidos-alpha/kernel/rk3566-ampheck-eidos-alpha.dts
  boards/ampheck/eidos-alpha/kernel/patches/6.1/

The kernel and every driver included in that source tree retain their upstream
copyrights and per-file licenses. Most kernel files are licensed under
GPL-2.0-only or GPL-2.0+, as identified by their SPDX headers. UAPI headers may
instead use GPL-2.0+ WITH Linux-syscall-note or a GPL-2.0+/MIT dual license as
stated in the relevant file. The board device tree is dual-licensed under
GPL-2.0+ OR MIT. Ampheck-authored build integration is Apache-2.0. The
board kernel patches modify GPL-2.0-only or GPL-2.0+ kernel code and remain
under the license of the affected source files.

The Rockchip boot-mode integration patch under common/uboot/patches is
Ampheck-authored and remains under U-Boot's GPL-2.0+ license.

